 34AL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34AL c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2017Ch36:                          
 34AL2c  Phys Rev C 96, 034301 (2017)                                           
 34AL c  Compiled by: J. Chen (NSCL/MSU), September 20, 2017                    
 34AL c  Coulomb dissociation of {+35}Al using a Pb target                      
 34AL c  2017Ch36: {+35}Al ions were produced by fragmentation of a 531         
 34AL2c  MeV/nucleon {+40}Ar beam provided by the Heavy Ion Synchrotron (SIS18) 
 34AL3c  at GSI. The fragments were separated by the FRagment Separator (FRS)   
 34AL4c  according to magnetic rigidity. The secondary target was 2 g/cm{+2}    
 34AL5c  lead. Heavy breakup fragments were detected by 8 DSSSDs and            
 34AL6c  separated by a large-area dipole magnet (ALADIN) and tracked using two 
 34AL7c  large scintillator fiber detectors (GFIs); breakup neutrons were       
 34AL8c  detected by the high-efficiency Large Area Neutron Detector (LAND); |g 
 34AL9c  rays were detected with a spherical 4|p Crystal Ball detector array of 
 34ALac  162 NaI(Tl) crystals. Measured E(fragment), E(n), E|g, Coulomb         
 34ALbc  dissociation cross sections. Deduced levels, relative populations, g.s.
 34ALcc  configuration of {+35}Al. Comparisons with available data and          
 34ALdc  shell-model calculations.                                              
 34AL cG E$From level-energy difference, as indicated in Fig. 2(c) of 2017Ch36  
 34AL cL $Partial level scheme and half-lives are as given in 2017Ch36, taken   
 34AL2cL from 2017Li03: Phys Rev C 95, 021301(R) (2017), unless otherwise noted.
 34AL3cL Energy values are rounded-off values.                                  
 34AL cL $The total measured inclusive differential Coulomb dissociation cross  
 34AL2cL section is 78 mb {I13}, integrated up to 5.0 MeV relative energy       
 34AL3cL between the {+34}Al core and the neutron using a Pb target.            
